# Agents on Apps Project Architecture

This is an experimental Databricks project for deploying agents on Databricks Apps instead of Model Serving.

## Project Structure

The repository contains two main agent implementations:

### 1. responses-api-agent
- **Backend**: Python FastAPI server in [responses-api-agent/src/agent_server/](mdc:responses-api-agent/src/agent_server/)
- **Frontend**: React/TypeScript UI in [responses-api-agent/ui/](mdc:responses-api-agent/ui/)
- **Main entry point**: [responses-api-agent/src/agent_server/agent.py](mdc:responses-api-agent/src/agent_server/agent.py)
- **Server**: [responses-api-agent/src/agent_server/server.py](mdc:responses-api-agent/src/agent_server/server.py)

### 2. non-conversational-agent  
- **Backend only**: Python implementation in [non-conversational-agent/src/agent_server/](mdc:non-conversational-agent/src/agent_server/)
- **Main entry point**: [non-conversational-agent/src/agent_server/agent.py](mdc:non-conversational-agent/src/agent_server/agent.py)

## Key Features
- Built-in MLflow tracing and logging
- Async FastAPI server with `/invocations` endpoint
- Streaming and non-streaming responses
- Unity Catalog function toolkit integration
- Vector search retriever tools
- React UI with real-time chat interface

## Development Flow
1. Agents are implemented by extending `ResponsesAgent` class
2. Tools are registered via `ToolInfo` objects and `TOOL_INFOS` list
3. Server decorators `@invoke()` and `@stream()` register endpoints
4. Frontend communicates via `/invocations` endpoint

## Configuration Files
- [pyproject.toml](mdc:responses-api-agent/pyproject.toml): Python dependencies
- [package.json](mdc:responses-api-agent/ui/package.json): Frontend dependencies  
- [app.yaml](mdc:responses-api-agent/app.yaml): Databricks App deployment config